---
source: crates/dffy/src/config.rs
expression: text
---
<dim># Color output: auto, always or never. With auto, NO_COLOR and CLICOLOR_FORCE apply.</>
<hint>color</><dim> = </>auto

<dim># Page output on a terminal: auto, always or never. Auto prints a piped diff that fits one screen; always opens the viewer for it.</>
<hint>paging</><dim> = </>auto

<dim># Pager command, run through sh. Empty uses $PAGER, then less -RFX. DFFY_PAGER overrides it.</>
<hint>pager</><dim> = </>

<dim># Theme name: a built-in or a file in the themes directory next to this file.</>
<hint>theme</><dim> = </>default

<dim># Diff layout: auto, split or unified. Auto splits on terminals at least split-min-width wide.</>
<hint>view</><dim> = </>auto

<dim># How changed lines are marked besides their color: background (a tint behind the line and a stronger one behind its numbers), bars (a colored bar in the gutter), classic (+ and - signs) or none. Auto picks background on truecolor terminals (COLORTERM=truecolor or 24bit) and bars otherwise. Without color, classic signs are always used so the output stays a readable diff.</>
<hint>indicators</><dim> = </>auto

<dim># How a changed line is colored when it pairs with the line it was edited into: changed (both lines in the modified color, theme keys `modified`, `modified-line` and `modified-number`, with only the edited tokens in red and green) or added-removed (a red line and a green one, as for lines wholly removed or added). Lines without a partner are red or green either way. --color-only keeps red and green.</>
<hint>modified-lines</><dim> = </>changed

<dim># The terminal's background for the tints of indicators = background: auto, dark or light. Auto starts dark and asks the terminal (OSC 11), switching to light tints if it answers within 200ms; printed output uses dark.</>
<hint>background</><dim> = </>auto

<dim># Terminal width in columns from which view = auto picks the split layout.</>
<hint>split-min-width</><dim> = </>140

<dim># Wrap long lines instead of truncating them.</>
<hint>wrap</><dim> = </>false

<dim># Columns per tab stop.</>
<hint>tab-width</><dim> = </>4

<dim># Lines of context around each change (-U), or full for the whole file with changes inline. In the viewer, `X` switches every file between the two and is remembered; `x` reveals hidden lines in one file, for that run.</>
<hint>context</><dim> = </>3

<dim># Ignore all whitespace when comparing lines (-w). The command panel's Ignore whitespace entry toggles it in the viewer.</>
<hint>ignore-all-space</><dim> = </>false

<dim># Ignore changes in the amount of whitespace (-b). The command panel's Ignore whitespace entry switches between ignoring all whitespace and none.</>
<hint>ignore-space-change</><dim> = </>false

<dim># What dffy without revisions shows: all (everything not committed: HEAD against the working tree, with staged, unstaged and untracked files, each file marked by its staging) or unstaged (the working tree against the index, as plain git diff, which hides staged and untracked files; the same as --unstaged). --staged and revisions are unaffected.</>
<hint>default-diff</><dim> = </>all

<dim># Detect renames as git diff -M does. Printed output waits for the rename pass when there are both added and deleted files; the viewer shows them unpaired first.</>
<hint>renames</><dim> = </>true

<dim># Syntax-highlight code in diffs (with color on). Files over 512KB are never highlighted.</>
<hint>highlight</><dim> = </>true

<dim># Diff code by syntax: emphasize only changed tokens (reordered arguments included), dim code that was only reformatted (~) and mark whole statements or items that moved (», theme key `moved`). `d` toggles it in the viewer. Files over 2MB or in unknown languages keep the line diff.</>
<hint>syntax-diff</><dim> = </>false

<dim># Experimental: renderer plugins by file extension, as space-separated extension:name pairs (md:markdown csv:csv). A file of a listed type can show rendered in the viewer, with `r`, by the program dffy-render-<name> on PATH, which is looked up and run only then. See docs/plugins.md.</>
<hint>render</><dim> = </>

<dim># Show files that have a renderer (see render) rendered in the viewer, diffed block by block, instead of as lines; `r` toggles it.</>
<hint>rendered</><dim> = </>false

<dim># Experimental: the review plugin, the program dffy-review-<name> on PATH. It adds the command it names to open one of the code host's reviews in the viewer, and plain `dffy` asks it for the branch's. auto uses the only such program on PATH, and no plugin when there are several (dffy doctor lists them). none, or empty, means no plugin and no such command. --review <name|auto|none> sets it for one run. See docs/plugins.md.</>
<hint>review</><dim> = </>auto

<dim># Experimental: which coding agent the agent plugin, dffy-agent on PATH, asks about a thread (`a`, or a comment starting @<name>), handed to it unread: claude, codex or pi picks the default, and a command with arguments, split at spaces, runs in their place with the prompt on its stdin. Empty leaves the pick to the plugin, Claude Code first. Fix with agent (`f`) starts the one this names of those the plugin can hand a thread to (claude, codex, pi or amp, when on PATH), else the first it lists. See docs/plugins.md.</>
<hint>agent</><dim> = </>

<dim># Start the viewer in watch mode, refreshing as files, the index or refs change; `w` toggles it. With nothing to show, a watching viewer opens and waits for changes instead of printing that there are none.</>
<hint>watch</><dim> = </>false

<dim># Whether the viewer starts with the file tree: auto shows it on terminals at least 100 columns wide, show also opens it on narrower ones, over the diff, and hide starts without it. `t` and `T` toggle it; a `show` remembered from a wide terminal doesn't open it over the diff on a narrow one.</>
<hint>tree</><dim> = </>auto

<dim># The tree's width in columns, or auto for 28% of the terminal (24 to 60 columns). `+` and `-` in the tree change it.</>
<hint>tree-width</><dim> = </>auto

<dim># Where the viewer shows what's compared, the position, the modes and the key hints: bottom (in the frame's bottom border) or top (in its top border, after the file's name). The command panel's Status bar entry switches it.</>
<hint>status-bar</><dim> = </>bottom

<dim># Show line numbers, in the viewer and in printed diffs. Without them the change marks stay.</>
<hint>line-numbers</><dim> = </>true

<dim># Show the @@ -a,b +c,d @@ numbers of hunks; without them a hunk shows only its function and the ⋯ N unchanged lines before it.</>
<hint>hunk-headers</><dim> = </>true

<dim># Copies from the viewer include each line's number and its +/- sign, for pasting into a review, rather than only the code.</>
<hint>copy-decorations</><dim> = </>false

<dim># Remember the view choices made in the viewer (layout, wrap, the tree and its width, the status bar, indicators, modified lines, syntax diff, rendered view, highlighting, theme, mouse, line numbers, hunk headers, copy decorations, whole files, ignored whitespace, watch mode) for the next run, in $XDG_STATE_HOME/dffy/state. A choice made in the viewer beats this file in the viewer; a flag beats both, for that run only. Printed output never takes them. A remembered split layout shows unified under 100 columns; --split doesn't.</>
<hint>remember</><dim> = </>true

<dim># Show the one-time tip about the command panel on the first run of the viewer.</>
<hint>tips</><dim> = </>true

<dim># Take mouse input in the viewer: clicks, the wheel, and dragging over code to select and copy it. The command panel's Mouse selection entry turns it off for the terminal's own selection (many terminals, Ghostty included, also select natively with shift held while dragging).</>
<hint>mouse</><dim> = </>true

<dim># Keep results that are slow to compute (renames, highlighting of large files) in $XDG_CACHE_HOME/dffy.</>
<hint>cache</><dim> = </>true

<dim># Size the disk cache is trimmed to, least recently used first: bytes, or a number with K, M or G.</>
<hint>cache-size</><dim> = </>256M

<dim># Keys in the viewer: keybind = <key>=<action>, or <key>=unbind to free a key. A key is a character as typed (n, N, <, ?) or a name (space, enter, tab, shift+tab, esc, backspace, up, down, left, right, home, end, page_up, page_down, insert, delete, f1 to f12), with ctrl+ or alt+ before it. Keys pressed in the file tree look in its own table first, set with tree: before the key (keybind = tree:v=mark_viewed), and so do keys pressed while a comment thread is focused, in the thread's table (thread:), then while the file at the cursor has conflicts to resolve, in the conflict's table (conflict:). The command panel the leader key opens has its own table too, set with leader: (keybind = leader:z=toggle_wrap); within a group, the panel lists its entries in this order.</>

<dim># leader: open the command panel; its next key runs a command</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>space=leader

<dim># scroll_down: scroll down a line; in the tree, move down</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>j=scroll_down
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>down=scroll_down
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>enter=scroll_down
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>ctrl+e=scroll_down
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>ctrl+n=scroll_down

<dim># scroll_up: scroll up a line; in the tree, move up</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>k=scroll_up
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>up=scroll_up
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>ctrl+y=scroll_up
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>ctrl+p=scroll_up

<dim># page_down: scroll down a screen</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>page_down=page_down
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>ctrl+f=page_down

<dim># page_up: scroll up a screen</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>b=page_up
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>page_up=page_up
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>ctrl+b=page_up

<dim># half_page_down: scroll down half a screen</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>ctrl+d=half_page_down

<dim># half_page_up: scroll up half a screen</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>ctrl+u=half_page_up

<dim># top: top of the file</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>g=top
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>home=top

<dim># bottom: bottom of the file</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>G=bottom
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>end=bottom

<dim># next_change: next change, on into the next file</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>n=next_change
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>}=next_change

<dim># prev_change: previous change, back into the previous file</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>N=prev_change
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>{=prev_change

<dim># next_file: next file</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>f=next_file
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>]=next_file
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>alt+f=next_file
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>alt+right=next_file
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:f=next_file

<dim># prev_file: previous file</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>F=prev_file
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>[=prev_file
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>alt+b=prev_file
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>alt+left=prev_file
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:F=prev_file

<dim># expand: show more of the highlighted ⋯ gap</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>x=expand
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:x=expand

<dim># toggle_full: whole files or changes only, for every file</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>X=toggle_full
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:X=toggle_full

<dim># scroll_right: scroll the code right, without wrapping</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>>=scroll_right
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>L=scroll_right

<dim># scroll_left: scroll the code left</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </><=scroll_left
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>H=scroll_left

<dim># scroll_reset: scroll the code back to its first column</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>0=scroll_reset

<dim># select: select lines, from the top line or the one tapped</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>v=select

<dim># copy: copy the selected lines' code</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>y=copy
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:y=copy

<dim># copy_path: copy the file's path</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>Y=copy_path
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:Y=copy_path

<dim># copy_absolute_path: copy where the file is on disk, from the filesystem's root</>
<dim># (no key by default)</>

<dim># copy_comment: copy a comment of the focused thread as written, in Markdown: the one last clicked, else its first</>
<dim># (no key by default)</>

<dim># copy_thread: copy the focused thread: each comment under its author and date, as written</>
<dim># (no key by default)</>

<dim># copy_prompt: copy the focused thread, else the selected lines, as a prompt for a coding agent: the comments, the lines with those around them and the file's changes near them</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>thread:y=copy_prompt
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:"=copy_prompt

<dim># cancel: end the selection; in the tree, clear the filter</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>esc=cancel

<dim># switch_pane: switch between the left panel (the file tree, or the comments) and the diff</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>tab=switch_pane
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>shift+tab=switch_pane

<dim># toggle_tree: show or hide the file tree</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>T=toggle_tree
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>t=toggle_tree
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:t=toggle_tree

<dim># open_picker: find a file: type part of its path, enter opens it</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>o=open_picker
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:o=open_picker

<dim># search: search the diff's text; n/N then go between matches, esc clears</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>/=search

<dim># filter_tree: filter the file tree, fuzzily; f/F and n/N keep to the files it keeps, esc clears</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>tree:/=filter_tree
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:|=filter_tree

<dim># open: open a file, or open or close a folder, in the tree</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>tree:enter=open
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>tree:l=open
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>tree:right=open

<dim># collapse: collapse a folder in the tree</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>tree:h=collapse
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>tree:left=collapse

<dim># parent_folder: go to the folder holding the file, in the tree</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>u=parent_folder

<dim># mark_viewed: mark a file in the tree viewed</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>tree:v=mark_viewed

<dim># tree_wider: widen the tree</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>tree:+=tree_wider

<dim># tree_narrower: narrow the tree</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>tree:-=tree_narrower

<dim># cycle_layout: layout: split, unified, then auto (split on wide screens); while selecting, the side copied</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>s=cycle_layout
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:s=cycle_layout

<dim># toggle_wrap: wrap or truncate long lines</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>W=toggle_wrap
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:W=toggle_wrap

<dim># toggle_syntax: diff by lines or by syntax</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>d=toggle_syntax
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:d=toggle_syntax

<dim># toggle_rendered: files with a renderer plugin rendered, or as lines (experimental, see render)</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>r=toggle_rendered
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:r=toggle_rendered

<dim># cycle_indicators: how changed lines are marked: background, bars, classic signs or none</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:K=cycle_indicators

<dim># cycle_modified_lines: a line and its edit in the modified color with red and green tokens, or red and green lines</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:%=cycle_modified_lines

<dim># toggle_highlight: syntax highlighting on or off</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:*=toggle_highlight

<dim># toggle_whitespace: ignore whitespace (-w) or not, diffing again</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:I=toggle_whitespace

<dim># toggle_line_numbers: show or hide line numbers</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:#=toggle_line_numbers

<dim># toggle_hunk_headers: show or hide the @@ numbers of hunks</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:@=toggle_hunk_headers

<dim># toggle_status_bar: the status bar in the frame's bottom border or its top one</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:B=toggle_status_bar

<dim># cycle_theme: the next theme, built-in or yours</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:~=cycle_theme

<dim># toggle_watch: watch for changes</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>w=toggle_watch
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:w=toggle_watch

<dim># take_checkpoint: take a checkpoint of the working tree: its files as plain dffy lists them, staged or not and untracked, kept under a local ref of this worktree, the last 5 of them; starting Fix with agent takes one too</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:;=take_checkpoint

<dim># since_checkpoint: show only what changed since the latest checkpoint, such as an agent's turn since Fix with agent started it, or the diff shown before again; the status bar says how long ago it was taken</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>'=since_checkpoint
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:'=since_checkpoint

<dim># toggle_mouse: take mouse input, or leave it to the terminal's own selection (many terminals select natively with shift held while dragging)</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:$=toggle_mouse

<dim># toggle_copy_decorations: copies include line numbers and +/- signs, or only the code</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:J=toggle_copy_decorations

<dim># stage: stage the selected lines, else the hunk of the line last tapped or the first on screen: their working-tree version goes in the index (uncommitted changes only)</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>A=stage
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:A=stage

<dim># unstage: unstage the selected lines, else the hunk of the line last tapped or the first on screen: their HEAD version goes back in the index (uncommitted changes only)</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>U=unstage
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:U=unstage

<dim># discard: discard the selected lines' unstaged changes, else the hunk's, after a y/n: the working tree gets back the index's version, and an untracked file is deleted (uncommitted changes only)</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>D=discard
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:D=discard

<dim># next_conflict: in a conflicted file, the next conflict</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>conflict:n=next_conflict

<dim># prev_conflict: in a conflicted file, the previous conflict</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>conflict:N=prev_conflict

<dim># keep_current: resolve the conflict last gone to, else the first on screen, to the current side (ours); again takes the choice back. Choices show as a preview until written</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>conflict:o=keep_current

<dim># take_incoming: resolve the conflict to the incoming side (theirs); again takes the choice back</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>conflict:t=take_incoming

<dim># keep_both: resolve the conflict to both sides, the current one first; again takes the choice back</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>conflict:b=keep_both

<dim># take_base: resolve the conflict to the common ancestor's lines, when git wrote them (merge.conflictStyle diff3 or zdiff3); again takes the choice back</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>conflict:a=take_base

<dim># write_resolution: write the conflicted file as the choices resolve it, asking first when some conflicts have none; then git add it after a y/n</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>conflict:w=write_resolution

<dim># edit: open the file in $EDITOR at the line last tapped, else the top line</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>e=edit

<dim># open_terminal: open a new tab in your terminal, or a window where that's all it offers, at the working tree's root; where dffy can't, it copies a cd there instead</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:.=open_terminal

<dim># comment: comment on the selected lines, or the line v would start on, in a text box under them; enter sends it</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>c=comment

<dim># suggest_change: suggest a change to the selected lines, or the line v would start on: a comment's text box holding them, to edit into what they should be; enter sends it</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>S=suggest_change
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:S=suggest_change

<dim># comment_file: comment on the whole file shown, in a text box under its first row; enter sends it</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>C=comment_file

<dim># comments: the left panel lists every comment thread in place of the files, or the files again; moving through the threads shows each in the diff, enter or tab goes to it; the thread keys act on the selected thread, and c filters them by state</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>i=comments
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:i=comments

<dim># next_thread: next comment thread, on into the next file with comments; it takes the focus, where r replies, e edits, x resolves, d deletes and o opens it on its host</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>m=next_thread

<dim># prev_thread: previous comment thread, back into the previous file with comments</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>M=prev_thread

<dim># toggle_thread: fold or unfold the focused comment thread, or the first on screen</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>z=toggle_thread

<dim># toggle_threads: fold every comment thread to one row, or unfold them all</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>Z=toggle_threads

<dim># move_thread: move the focused thread, or the comments panel's selected one, from the branch it was written on to the current branch</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>V=move_thread

<dim># ask_agent: ask a coding agent, through the agent plugin dffy-agent, about the focused thread: write your question in a reply box, which enter sends with the thread to the agent that answered last, else the default one; enter on the empty box asks about the thread as it is, and esc keeps the question without asking. Elsewhere, write the question on the selected lines, or the line v would start on, in a text box, and enter asks. The answer comes as the agent's reply, with a suggestion when it proposes a change; esc on the thread stops it. A comment you write starting @ and an agent's name, as @name, asks that agent too (experimental, see agent)</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>a=ask_agent
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>thread:a=ask_agent
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:a=ask_agent

<dim># reply: on a thread: reply in a text box under it; enter sends it</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>thread:r=reply

<dim># edit_draft: on a thread: edit your last draft in it, in a text box; enter sends it</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>thread:e=edit_draft

<dim># delete_draft: on a thread: delete your last draft in it, the whole thread when that's its first comment or the thread is resolved with nothing on the host, once the key comes again</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>thread:d=delete_draft

<dim># resolve: on a thread: resolve it, or reopen it</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>thread:x=resolve

<dim># adopt: on a thread: someone else's comments in it not posted, as an agent's, become your drafts, which posting sends under your name</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>thread:A=adopt

<dim># apply_suggestion: on a thread: put its suggestion, the one last clicked or else its last, in place of the lines it's on in the working tree, refused when they changed since; an unstaged change, which discard undoes. On one applied already, put back the lines it replaced</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>thread:s=apply_suggestion

<dim># fix_with_agent: on a thread, or the selected lines with a note you write first: start your coding agent in a new tab, or here until it exits, pointed at the thread to change what it asks and reply in it</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>thread:f=fix_with_agent
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:&=fix_with_agent

<dim># send_open_threads: take a checkpoint, then start your coding agent as fix with agent does, pointed at every open thread of yours in view (those you started or replied in) to change what each asks and reply in each; since checkpoint then shows its turn</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:^=send_open_threads

<dim># open_on_host: on a thread: open it on its code host, in the browser</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>thread:o=open_on_host

<dim># clear_resolved: delete the resolved threads shown, after a y/n; on a code host's review only what isn't posted, as the host's threads would come back</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:-=clear_resolved

<dim># comment_in_editor: write in $EDITOR: your draft in the focused thread, else a reply to it, else a comment on the line; ctrl+g does it from the text box</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>E=comment_in_editor
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:E=comment_in_editor

<dim># commented_files: the tree shows only the files with comments, or every file; f/F and n/N keep to them. In the comments panel, it steps through all threads, open ones, drafts and resolved ones, and its capital steps back</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>tree:c=commented_files
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:!=commented_files

<dim># review_pull: on a review a review plugin opened, fetch its new commits and threads and show them in place (experimental, see review)</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>p=review_pull

<dim># review_post: on a review a review plugin opened, open the dialog that posts your drafts, replies and resolves as a review (experimental, see review)</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>P=review_post

<dim># open_review: list the reviews the review plugin offers, such as this branch's, yours and those waiting on you, to open one (experimental, see review)</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>O=open_review
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:O=open_review

<dim># since_last_review: on a review a review plugin opened, show only what changed since the head of your last review, as the review plugin records it, or the whole review again</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>R=since_last_review
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:R=since_last_review

<dim># whole_review: on the branch's review that plain dffy found, show the whole review against the working tree, or the working tree's changes again</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:Q=whole_review

<dim># help: show or hide this help</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>?=help
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>leader:?=help

<dim># quit: quit</>
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>q=quit
<hint>keybind</><dim> = </>ctrl+c=quit
